/**
 * Extended botanical/reference profile data for the Plant Database
 * (/plants/). Kept as a companion file keyed by plants.js id — the same
 * pattern already established by plant-yields.js, plant-spacing.js, and
 * planting-windows.js — rather than expanding the 185-entry plants.js
 * file directly, so the core wizard-matching schema stays untouched.
 *
 * Compiled reference data (standard horticultural/botanical knowledge —
 * scientific names, native range, ASPCA-style pet toxicity, bloom
 * characteristics, harvest pattern, traditional/folk medicinal use where
 * well-documented), not scraped from any source. Field notes:
 *
 * - scientificName: genus + species binomial (or "Genus spp." for a
 *   plant sold/grown as many interchangeable species/cultivars, e.g.
 *   Hosta, Salvia, Echeveria)
 * - lifecycle: 'annual' | 'perennial' | 'biennial' — as COMMONLY GROWN by
 *   home gardeners (e.g. tomato and basil are botanically tender
 *   perennials but grown as annuals almost everywhere outside the
 *   tropics; this matches how the rest of the site already frames zones
 *   and seasons)
 * - nativeRange: region-level, not country-precise
 * - toxicity: { petSafe: boolean|null (null = data genuinely mixed/part-
 *   dependent), notes } — pet-safety notes follow common ASPCA-style
 *   guidance; always advise checking with a vet for a specific case,
 *   never presented as a substitute for veterinary advice
 * - bloomColor: string, or null for plants grown for foliage/fruit/form
 *   rather than ornamental bloom
 * - bloomCycle: when/how it blooms
 * - harvestCycle: only meaningful for edible plants — 'single' (one
 *   harvest per planting, e.g. a head of cabbage), 'continuous' (cut-
 *   and-come-again over a season), or 'perennial' (established plant
 *   producing year after year); null for non-edible ornamentals
 * - medicinalBenefits: traditional/folk use, only populated where
 *   genuinely well-documented (many culinary herbs, a handful of
 *   vegetables/fruits) — null rather than fabricated for purely
 *   ornamental plants. Informational only, not medical advice; the same
 *   safety framing as guide-content/medicinal-herb-garden.js applies.
 */
